 ### 2D Banded Contouring
-Finds the 2D region where an interval $[L, H]$ of values exists. Each square corner is assigned a ternary value: 0 if value $< L$, 1 if $L \le value \le H$, 2 if value $> H$ [S3, unofficial]. This results in $3^4 = 81$ initial cases, reduced to 13 canonical cases after accounting for symmetries (rotational, mirror, high/low) [S3, unofficial]. The case number is determined by the base-3 number formed by the corner states [S3, unofficial].
